Requirements: 44   yielding obligations: 43   yielding none: 1

[task] `decompose` returns a flat list of obligations plus a flat list of open
    questions. A response covering 20 of a task file's 29 requirements is exactly as
    well-formed as one covering all 29, so nothing downstream can notice that nine
    requirements produced nothing. Gate 1 for #195 lost 4 of 15 Completion expectations
    and 5 of 8 Scope exclusions this way, and the review reported no gap.
    -> obligation-flat-obligations-and-open-questions  [functional/explicit]
       `decompose` returns two flat lists: one of obligations and one of open questions.
    -> obligation-no-missing-requirements-in-response  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-02)
       The response covers every requirement in the task file so that no requirement is
       left without a disposition.

[constraint-01] A requirement registry is derived from
    `requirement/task_file.py::parse_task_file`.
    -> obligation-requirement-registry-from-parse-task-file  [functional/explicit]
       Requirement registry derivation uses `requirement/task_file.py::parse_task_file`.

[constraint-02] Requirement ids are assigned by the code, never by the model.
    -> obligation-requirement-ids-assigned-by-code  [invariant/explicit]
       Requirement ids are assigned by the code rather than by the model.

[constraint-03] A requirement id is its section and its ordinal within that section, in
    parse order.
    -> obligation-requirement-id-section-ordinal-parse-order  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement id is formed from its section and its ordinal within that section,
       in parse order.

[constraint-04] Each registry entry carries the `TextSpan` of the requirement it
    identifies.
    -> obligation-registry-entry-carries-textspan  [invariant/explicit]
       Each registry entry includes the `TextSpan` for the requirement it identifies.

[constraint-05] The requirement-to-obligation relation is many-to-many.
    -> obligation-many-to-many-requirement-obligation-linking  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-07, completion-06)
       The requirement-to-obligation relation is many-to-many, so one obligation may
       serve multiple requirements and one requirement may relate to multiple
       obligations.

[constraint-06] An obligation serving two requirements is linked to both.
    -> obligation-obligation-linked-to-all-serving-requirements  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       An obligation that serves two requirements is linked to both requirements.

[constraint-07] An obligation is never duplicated so that each requirement can hold its
    own copy.
    -> obligation-many-to-many-requirement-obligation-linking  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-05, completion-06)
       The requirement-to-obligation relation is many-to-many, so one obligation may
       serve multiple requirements and one requirement may relate to multiple
       obligations.

[constraint-08] Every requirement carries exactly one disposition.
    -> obligation-one-disposition-per-requirement  [invariant/explicit]
       Every requirement has exactly one disposition.

[constraint-09] The dispositions are: yielded obligations; deliberately yields none,
    with a reason; raised an open question instead.
    -> obligation-disposition-kinds-yield-none-open-question  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       The disposition set consists of yielded obligations, deliberate no-obligation
       with a reason, or an open question.

[constraint-10] The mapping is persisted in the structured review state that
